 *
 * Language/runtime: JavaScript on Node.js (run `node --version`).  No external
 * packages; only Node core modules 'fs' (trace output) and 'child_process'/'os'
 * (parallel sweep driver, sweep.js) are used.
 *
 * Two equivalent step engines are provided:
 *   runFull  - literal full-scan transcription of Section 5 (reference)
 *   runFast  - event-driven candidate list, provably identical dynamics, ~10x faster
 * They are cross-checked by selftest; the Python ref_sim.py is a third check.
 *
 * Modes:
 *   node simulator.js baseline
 *   node simulator.js config <cycle> <plan> <lead|lag> <o0..o8>      (offsets in seconds)
 *   node simulator.js trace  <outfile>                               (baseline AM trace, uses runFast)
 *   node simulator.js selftest                                       (full vs fast on many configs)
 *   node simulator.js sweepchunk <prog> <offStart> <offEnd> <baseTTS>
